class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> shuffle(vector<int>& nums, int n) {
        vector<int> result;
        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            result.push_back(nums[i]);
            result.push_back(nums[i + n]);
        }
        return result;
    }
};
```

---

✅ **Explanation:**
- `nums[0..n-1]` → x1, x2, …, xn  
- `nums[n..2n-1]` → y1, y2, …, yn  
- The loop runs **n times**, each time pushing `xi` and `yi` alternately.  
- Time complexity: `O(n)`  
- Space complexity: `O(n)` for the `result` array.

